  "Question": "If \\(20 \\%\\) of a number is \\(12,\\) what is \\(30\\%\\) of the same number?",
  "Question Type": "text",
  "Choices": {
    "A": "\\(15\\)",
    "B": "\\(18\\)",
    "C": "\\(20\\)",
    "D": "\\(24\\)",
    "E": "\\(30\\)"
  },
  "Choices Type": "text",
  "Correct Answer": "B",
  "Solution": "Because both percentages refer to the same number, equal percentage shares have equal amounts. Half of \\(20\\%\\) is \\(10\\%\\), so \\(10\\%\\) of the number is \\(12\\div2=6\\).\n\nNow \\(30\\%\\) consists of three such shares, giving \\(3\\cdot6=18\\). The answer is \\(18\\), choice \\(B\\).",
